# Activate a pinned governance workflow after review

The template does not enable a workflow by default. After a baseline is reviewed,
merged and available at a known commit, add this caller using that full 40-character
SHA instead of `PIN_APPROVED_COMMIT`. Confirm private-repository workflow access
with the owner first. A valid-looking SHA alone is not proof of approval or access.

```yaml
name: Engineering Backbone
on:
  pull_request:
  push:
    branches: [{{ base_branch | tojson }}]
permissions:
  contents: read
jobs:
  governance:
    uses: Artifaktory/engineering-backbone/.github/workflows/governance-checks.yml@PIN_APPROVED_COMMIT
    permissions:
      contents: read
```

Alternatively, pass a reviewed SHA as `backbone_workflow_ref` during installation.
Existing `.github/workflows/engineering-backbone.yml` is preserved. Review and
activate it manually in the same adoption PR. There are no secrets or private source
checkout tokens in this workflow: it validates the caller's generated bundle.
Keep language-specific checks in the consuming project's existing CI.
